### Description

When balancer is selected as dialerProxy (via loopback) for the outbound with the reverse tag enabled, xray-core chooses one (sometimes two) random option from the selector list right at startup and then never changes it anymore. 
Restarting xray-core is the only effective way to rotate selector for given reverse outbound, regardless of the preferred strategy (Random, RoundRobin, or LeastLoad). 
Temporary forcing an override outbound from the 3X-UI balancer pane also has no effect. 
I’m not even sure that the fallback will be triggered when it necessary. 
Other (non-reverse) connections through the same balancer at the same time are handled as expected. 
Removing the reverse tag from that same outbound also makes balancer treat it as expected and rotate selector properly. 
So, only presence of the reverse tag breaks the selector rotation.

### Reproduction Method

Run **iftop** on the opposite side (i.e. public/portal) and observe your connections for more than a couple of minutes. Soon after the xray-core start up you will end up with one or two persistent IPs associated with the balancer.

